Since $14,600 is significantly higher than your $1,500 in itemized deductions, the standard deduction is the clear choice.

### 2. Home Office Deduction
You can deduct your home office expenses against your **freelance income** (not your W-2 income). 
*   **Business Percentage:** 170 sq ft / 720 sq ft = **23.61%** of your home.
*   **Actual Expenses Method:** 23.61% of your annual rent ($21,000) equals **$4,958.10**. You can also add 23.61% of your utilities and internet.
*   **Simplified Method:** 170 sq ft × $5/sq ft = **$850**.
